\v[1]" You came from \v[1], \v[2]."0Couldn't retrieve the location information."}Choose a destination.\ch[1,-1,Game Corner,Trainer area,Shadow Pokémon area,Bridges map,Water map, Harbour,Cycle Road,Cancel]"�The $Trainer global variable contains valuable information on the player, including their trainer type, ID, name, party Pokémon, money, and so on."@Refer to PokeBattle_Trainer for details on Trainer objects."]The Map Connector (also known as the Visual Editor) allows you to connect maps together."VIn the Debug menu (F9 or in the pause menu), choose the "Map Connections" option."�Once there, choose a map to display by pressing the S key. Select it and press the E key to edit its encounters, or double-click it to edit its metadata."�Add additional maps to the canvas by pressing the A key, and drag them around to connect them. Maps only connect if just their edges touch."}Every tile in a tileset has a terrain tag, which is a number. This number is used to give certain tiles special effects."�For example, ledge tiles have terrain tag 1, which means the player jumps over them. Ledge tiles also have a single passable direction (set separately)."qGrass tiles (in which you can have wild encounters) have terrain tag 2. Water tiles have terrain tag 6 or 7."�Terrain tag 0 means the tile has no special effect. See the wiki for more information and a complete list of all terrain tags and their effects."uTo set a tileset's terrain tags, open the Debug menu (F9 or from the pause menu) and choose "Edit Terrain Tags"."h\rThe "Choices" event command cannot allow more than 4 choices. This is what you should do instead."XPlease choose one.\ch[1,-1, Choice 1,Choice 2,Choice 3, Choice 4,Choice 5,Choice 6]"The choice was cancelled."Choice 1 was chosen."Choice 2 was chosen."Choice 3 was chosen."Choice 4 was chosen."Choice 5 was chosen."Choice 6 was chosen."PPlease choose one. This choice can't be canceled.\ch[1,0,Choice 1,Choice 2]"TMultiple choice commands like these are enabled using the \\ch message command."�The bracketed area after \\ch consists of the Variable to store the choice, a default choice in case the player cancels, and then a number of choices."@If the default choice is set to 0, the player can't cancel."\The $DEBUG flag was set. This flag is set automatically during playtesting within RMXP."{Debug mode allows you to access the Debug menu (F9 or in the pause menu), and to modify Pokémon in your party/the PC."xYou can also use hidden moves anytime, and hold CTRL to skip any battles and decide the outcome of Trainer battles.":Obtained all badges for the first and second regions."VTo add a badge, use $Trainer.badges[X]=true where X is a number from 0 through 7.">In Debug mode, you can set your badges in the Debug menu."/Press F8 to take a screenshot of the game."JThe screenshot will be put in the folder where the save file is kept."Choose a text option."V\bThis is the text of a male character. \rThis is the text of a female character."y\pgThis text is the colour of the player's gender. \pogThis text is the colour of the opposite gender to the player."�\c[0]Default text, \c[1]blue text, \c[2]red text, \c[3] green text, \c[4]cyan text, \c[5]magenta text, \c[6] yellow text, \c[7]grey text, \c[8]white text."�<b>Bold text,</b> <i>italic text,</i> <u>underlined text,</u> <s>strikethrough text,</s> <outln>outline text,</outln> <outln2>thicker outline text.</outln2>"u<fn=Arial>Arial text,</fn> <fs=25>size 25 text,</fs> <fs=40>size 40 text,</fs> <o=128>half-transparent text.</o>"�This is a line\n break. Text is \n<r>right-aligned until next line\n break. Text is <ac>centred</ac> here. Text is <ar>right-aligned</ar> here."_\PN is the player's name, \PM is the player's money, \v[12] is the content of Variable 12."!\GThe money window is shown.""\CNThe coins window is shown."\\G\CNThe money and coins windows are both shown. The coins window must be shown second."Q\f[introBoy]The introBoy picture from the Graphics/Pictures folder is shown."f\ff[introBoy]The introBoy picture is shown again, but cropped to the top-left 96x96 pixels of it."nThis is <icon=bagPocket3> bagPocket3 from the folder Graphics/Icons. Icons shown this way are not padded."?\w[signskin]The windowskin has changed to "signskin" here."�\l[3]This message box has 3 lines to it rather than 2, so more text can be shown at once. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipisicing elit."'\wuThis message box is at the top."*\wmThis message box is in the middle."X\wuThis message box is\wm jumping around the screen\wd in a rather off-putting way."7\opThis message box slides on-screen at the start."6\clThis message box slides off-screen at the end."'\ts[]This text appeared instantly!"\ts[5]This text is slow."5\se[itemlevel]Sound effect itemlevel was played."BMusic effect Jingle - HMTM will be played. \me[Jingle - HMTM]"EA complete list of all message options is available on the wiki."\PN received a Pokédex!"!You already have a Pokédex."*You don't have any Pokémon with you."/\v[2] is the first Pokémon in your party."%You have a Celebi in your party."+You don't have a Celebi in your party."{\rRemember to read the wiki for further information. An Internet shortcut to the wiki can be found in the main folder.")\PN obtained six different Pokémon."1Also received a Pokégear and Running Shoes."H\rOh... Are you all right? Well, you'll have better luck this time."}[This message was triggered by the "Starting Over" switch, which is currently set to true. Now turning that switch off.]"Choose a roaming Pokémon."4Switch 53 is on. Latias and Latios are roaming."eSwitch 53 is off. Latias and Latios are not roaming. Do you want to make Latias and Latios roam?"'Latias and Latios are now roaming."(Switch 54 is on. Kyogre is roaming."NSwitch 54 is off. Kyogre is not roaming. Do you want to make Kyogre roam?"Kyogre is now roaming."'Switch 55 is on. Entei is roaming."LSwitch 55 is off. Entei is not roaming. Do you want to make Entei roam?"Entei is now roaming."�Choose a destination.\ch[1,-1,Poké Center,Mart, Pokémon Gym,Day Care,Cave,Safari Zone, Bug Catching Contest,Battle Frontier,Cancel]"Voice Recorder"Download a file"Your real world location"Cancel"Yes"No"About the trainer"Map Connector"Terrain Tags"Debug mode"Give all badges"Taking screenshots"Colour and formatting"Showing extra things"
